  "conclusion": "In-model GEMM is 1.3-5.6x slower than the identical GEMM with resident weights, and even a per-call whole-weight copy variant stays 3.5x faster than in-model qkv. So the GEMM regions are limited by weight staging/lifecycle overlap, not by GEMM kernel efficiency. Closing that gap is worth about 3.7 s/step and is numerically free, which puts staging work (#4) ahead of GEMM layout work (#6).",
